/-!
# Definition 3.1 in DEC-146's form: nonsingular moves generating a group ergodic for λ

**`def:egf`** — `main.tex:216` (in its corrected form of record, DEC-146: C-26 with C-27; see SCOPE)

> Let $\Statespace$ be Riemannian manifold endowed with its volume measure $\lambda$ and let
> $(\Phi_{i})_{i=1}^p$ be a family of diffeomorphisms $\Statespace\rightarrow \Statespace$. An EGF
> is a generative flow, where
> $\ForwardPolicyStar(s) = \sum_{i=1}^p\forwardalpha^i(s) \delta_{\Phi_i(s)}$
> for some policy $\forwardalpha:\Statespace \rightarrow [0,1]^p$, and such that the group of
> diffeomorphisms generated by the $\Phi_i$ is topologically ergodic. That is for all
> $x,y \in \Statespace$ and any neighborhood $\mathcal U$ of $y$, there exists a sequence
> $i_1,\cdots, i_t$ such that $x\Phi_{i_1}\Phi_{i_2}\cdots \Phi_{i_t} \in \mathcal U$.
> (`main.tex:216–222`)

The corrected text of record (`papers/egf/programme/corrections.toml`, C-27 then C-26, DEC-146),
replacing l.219–221 from "for some policy":

> for some measurable policy $\forwardalpha:\Statespace\rightarrow[0,1]^p$ with
> $\sum_i\forwardalpha^i=1$, and such that the group of diffeomorphisms generated by the $\Phi_i$
> is ergodic for $\lambda$. That is, every measurable $A\subset\Statespace$ with
> $\lambda\left(\Phi_i^{-1}(A)\,\triangle\,A\right)=0$ for all $i$ satisfies $\lambda(A)=0$ or
> $\lambda(\Statespace\setminus A)=0$.

## What is defined and proved

| | |
|---|---|
| `egfGroup`, **`IsEGFErgodic`**, `isEGFErgodic_iff_symmDiff`, `IsEGFErgodic.inflowAC` | the group generated by the moves; `def:egf` (fields `policy`, `nonsingular`, `ergodic`); the corrected text word for word; `F_in ≪ λ` (C-6) |
| `ae_invariant_of_mem_closure_of_quasi`, `isGroupErgodic_egfGroup_iff` | the generator form of the "that is" equals the group form for nonsingular moves; `FourCycle.isGroupErgodic_not_forall`: not without |
| `IsEGFPolicy.isKernelErgodic_iff`, `isEGFErgodic_iff_isKernelErgodic` | positive weights: the clause is the ergodicity of the kernel |
| `IsEGFErgodic.isUniversalPolicy`, `isEGFErgodic_iff_isUniversalPolicy`, `IsEGFErgodic.isUniversalFamilyEps` | the clause is what Theorem B.1 / 3.4 under ergodicity (C-29) need, and all they need |
| `isUniversalFamilyEps_of_isGroupErgodic`, `universality_of_isEGFErgodic`, `isUniversalFamilyEps_iff_forall_isEGFErgodic` | measure-preserving moves, uniform policy: ε-universal iff the group is ergodic iff every member is an EGF |
| `nonsingular_of_measurePreserving`, `nonsingular_of_diffeomorph`, `isEGFErgodic_diffeomorph_iff` | instances of the `nonsingular` field; on `ℝᵈ` with Lebesgue measure it is automatic |
| `AffineToroidalModel.isEGFErgodic_flow_iff`, `isEGFErgodic_torus_iff`, `IsometrySphericalModel.isEGFErgodic_flow_iff`, `isEGFErgodic_sphere_iff` | the families of tori and spheres are EGFs iff their groups are ergodic |
| `isEGFErgodic_sphere_two_witness`, `isEGFErgodic_circleRotFlow_iff`, `isEGFErgodic_circleRotFlow_sqrt_two`, `Swap.isEGFErgodic_flow` | inhabitants: a rotation of `𝕊¹`, of the circle (iff of infinite order), the swap |
