## Hypothesis checklist

| paper (`main.tex:217–221`, C-26, C-27) | here (`IsEGFErgodic lam F Φ α`) |
|---|---|
| `𝒮` a Riemannian manifold, `λ` its volume | ⚠ weakened: any measurable space, any measure `λ` |
| `Φᵢ` diffeomorphisms | ⚠ weakened: measurable equivalences `𝒮 ≃ᵐ 𝒮` preserving the `λ`-null sets both ways (field `nonsingular`), the property diffeomorphisms have for the volume; automatic for `Cⁿ` diffeomorphisms (`n ≥ 1`) and Haar measure (`isEGFErgodic_diffeomorph_iff`), affine maps of tori, rotations of spheres |
| `α : 𝒮 → [0,1]^p`, `π(s) = ∑ᵢ αⁱ(s) δ_{Φᵢ(s)}`, a generative flow | ✓ C-27: `IsEGFPolicy F.policy` (`α` measurable, `≥ 0`, `∑ᵢ αⁱ = 1`), `F : GenerativeFlow 𝒮` |
| the group generated by the `Φᵢ` ergodic for `λ` (DEC-146) | ✓ `IsGroupErgodic lam (egfGroup Φ)`; C-26's "that is" (`λ(Φᵢ⁻¹A ∆ A) = 0 ∀ i`) is equivalent (`isEGFErgodic_iff_symmDiff`) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

`def:egf` is marked in DEC-146's corrected form (C-26, C-27): neither topological reading is of
record (DEC-146); both stay in `EGF.Defs` (`IsEGF` with `IsTopologicallyErgodic`, the forward-word
clause; `IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup`, the group reading; `shiftZ_group_not_forward`). Reading
taken (Mathlib has no Riemannian volume at the pin): the manifold, its volume and the
diffeomorphisms become `(𝒮, λ)` and measurable equivalences preserving `λ`-null sets both ways.
That diffeomorphisms of a Riemannian manifold do is standard and formalized here only for Haar
measure on a finite-dimensional space and for the measure-preserving moves of tori and spheres.
Not part of the definition: positive weights and a finite invariant `λ̂ ~ λ`, hypotheses of the
link to universality only. The witness of `isEGF_not_isEGFErgodic` uses
`λ = vol + ∑ₙ 2^{−e(n)} δ_{n•a}` (`e : ℤ ≃ ℕ`), not the volume (for the volume the same rotation
is an EGF); a minimal diffeomorphism not ergodic for the volume (Furstenberg, `𝕋²`) is not
formalized. The measure `δ_true` of `isEGFErgodic_not_isEGF` is not of full support. No `sorry`,
no axiom.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
